## Important Current Decisions

* OmniAskAI and APE remain separate products.
* OmniAskAI is initially one Next.js full-stack application.
* APE remains the only RAG/AI infrastructure layer.
* APE credentials are server-side only.
* Topic and APE Project remain separate concepts.
* Topic → APE Project mapping is stored on each revision in PostgreSQL and set from Admin. Seed does not read `APE_PROJECT_*` env vars.
* APE credentials and raw conversation ids stay server-side; the browser holds a sealed continuation token that contains the local conversation-reference ID.
* Public topic reads are request-scoped and uncached across requests.
* Topic behavior should be configuration-driven where practical.
* Public discovery and SEO are important product concerns.
* Prefer simple, explicit architecture over premature complexity.
* Admin authentication is Better Auth email/password with database sessions; bootstrap via `npm run admin:create`. Public signup is disabled.

